(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["text-structure-and-purpose_6"] = [{"id":"570970cd","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Indian Boyhood, a 1902 memoir by Ohiyesa (Charles A. Eastman), a Santee Dakota writer. In the text, Ohiyesa recalls how the women in his tribe harvested maple syrup during his childhood. Now the women began to test the trees — moving leisurely among them, axe in hand, and striking a single quick blow, to see if the sap would appear. The trees, like people, have their individual characters; some were ready to yield up their life-blood, while others were more reluctant. Now one of the birchen basins was set under each tree, and a hardwood chip driven deep into the cut which the axe had made. From the corners of this chip— — at first drop by drop, then more freely the sap trickled into the little dishes.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Indian Boyhood, a 1902 memoir by Ohiyesa (Charles A. Eastman), a Santee Dakota writer. In the text, Ohiyesa","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"recalls how the women in his tribe harvested maple syrup during his childhood.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Now the women began to test the trees—moving leisurely among them, axe in hand, and striking a single quick blow, to see if the sap would","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"appear. The trees, like people, have their individual characters; some were ready to yield up their life-blood, while others were more reluctant.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Now one of the birchen basins was set under each tree, and a hardwood chip driven deep into the cut which the axe had made. From the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"corners of this chip—at first drop by drop, then more freely—the sap trickled into the little dishes.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It portrays the range of personality traits displayed by the women as they work.","It foregrounds the beneficial relationship between humans and maple trees.","It demonstrates how human behavior can be influenced by the natural environment.","It elaborates on an aspect of the maple trees that the women evaluate."],"underline":"The trees, like people, have their individual characters; some were ready to yield up their life-blood, while others were more reluctant.","underline_segments":["The trees, like people, have their individual characters; some were ready to yield up their life-blood, while others were more reluctant."]},{"id":"03c9f327","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Charlotte Brontë s 1847 novel Jane Eyre. Jane, the narrator, works as a governess at Thornfield Hall. I went on with my day’s business tranquilly; but ever and anon vague suggestions kept wandering across my brain of reasons why I should quit Thornfield; and I kept involuntarily framing advertisements and pondering conjectures about new situations: these thoughts I did not think to check; they might germinate and bear fruit if they could.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Charlotte Brontë’s 1847 novel Jane Eyre. Jane, the narrator, works as a governess at Thornfield Hall.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I went on with my day’s business tranquilly; but ever and anon vague suggestions kept wandering across my brain of reasons why I should quit","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Thornfield; and I kept involuntarily framing advertisements and pondering conjectures about new situations: these thoughts I did not think to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"check; they might germinate and bear fruit if they could.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To convey a contrast between Jane’s outward calmness and internal restlessness","To emphasize Jane’s loyalty to the people she works for at Thornfield Hall","To demonstrate that Jane finds her situation both challenging and deeply fulfilling","To describe Jane’s determination to secure employment outside of Thornfield Hall"]},{"id":"6f5fc289","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Charles Dickens’s 1854 novel Hard Times. Coketown is a fictional town in England. [Coketown] contained several large streets all very like one another, and many small streets still more like one another, inhabited by people equally like one another, who all went in and out at the same hours, with the same sound upon the same pavements, to do the same work, and to whom every day was the same as yesterday and tomorrow, and every year the counterpart of the last and the next.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Charles Dickens’s 1854 novel Hard Times. Coketown is a fictional town in England.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"[Coketown] contained several large streets all very like one another, and many small streets still more like one another, inhabited by people","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"equally like one another, who all went in and out at the same hours, with the same sound upon the same pavements, to do the same work, and to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"whom every day was the same as yesterday and tomorrow, and every year the counterpart of the last and the next.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To emphasize the uniformity of both the town and the people who live there","To explain the limited work opportunities available to the town’s residents","To reveal how the predictability of the town makes it easy for people lose track of time","To argue that the simplicity of life in the town makes it a pleasant place to live"]},{"id":"4eee64fa","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Space scientists Anna-Lisa Paul, Stephen M. Elardo, and Robert Ferl planted seeds of Arabidopsis thaliana in samples of lunar regolith — the surface material of the Moon — and, serving as a control group, in terrestrial soil. They found that while all the seeds germinated, the roots of the regolith-grown plants were stunted compared with those in the control group. Moreover, unlike the plants in the control group, the regolith-grown plants exhibited red pigmentation, reduced leaf size, and inhibited growth rates — indicators of stress that were corroborated by postharvest molecular analysis.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Space scientists Anna-Lisa Paul, Stephen M. Elardo, and Robert Ferl planted seeds of Arabidopsis thaliana in samples of lunar regolith—the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"surface material of the Moon—and, serving as a control group, in terrestrial soil. They found that while all the seeds germinated, the roots of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"regolith-grown plants were stunted compared with those in the control group. Moreover, unlike the plants in the control group, the regolith-grown","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"plants exhibited red pigmentation, reduced leaf size, and inhibited growth rates—indicators of stress that were corroborated by postharvest","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"molecular analysis.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["It describes an experiment that addressed an unresolved question about the extent to which lunar regolith resembles terrestrial soils.","It compares two distinct methods of assessing indicators of stress in plants grown in a simulated lunar environment.","It presents evidence in support of the hypothesis that seed germination in lunar habitats is an unattainable goal.","It discusses the findings of a study that evaluated the effects of exposing a plant species to lunar soil conditions."]},{"id":"cce2f8dc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In 2023 literary scholar Jeremy Douglass cautioned technology investors and enthusiasts who predict conventional books’ ultimate displacement by newer forms of media. Douglass observed that the concept of an “interactive” text is much older than technologists assume, extending back to the first time readers scratched notes into a text’s margins. In addition, newer media, such as video games, haven’t replaced older forms of entertainment, such as comic books, but rather exist alongside them. Douglass believes that rather than supplanting books, technology is simply making new forms of expression possible.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2023 literary scholar Jeremy Douglass cautioned technology investors and enthusiasts who predict conventional books’ ultimate","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"displacement by newer forms of media. Douglass observed that the concept of an “interactive” text is much older than technologists assume,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"extending back to the first time readers scratched notes into a text’s margins. In addition, newer media, such as video games, haven’t replaced","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"older forms of entertainment, such as comic books, but rather exist alongside them. Douglass believes that rather than supplanting books,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"technology is simply making new forms of expression possible.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It challenges the stance of the investors and enthusiasts who are mentioned earlier in the text.","It explains the basis for the claim made by the technologists mentioned in the text.","It suggests that academics are better suited than investors to see the potential uses of contemporary interactive texts.","It provides a historical anecdote about the technological challenges involved in reading the earliest interactive texts."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["the concept of an “interactive” text is much older than technologists assume,","extending back to the first time readers scratched notes into a text’s margins."]},{"id":"1782cdd7","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In many agricultural environments, the banks of streams are kept forested to protect water quality, but it’s been unclear what effects these forests may have on stream biodiversity. To investigate the issue, biologist Xingli Giam and colleagues studied an Indonesian oil palm plantation, comparing the species richness of forested streams with that of nonforested streams. Giam and colleagues found that species richness was significantly higher in forested streams, a finding the researchers attribute to the role leaf litter plays in sheltering fish from predators and providing food resources.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In many agricultural environments, the banks of streams are kept forested to protect water quality, but it’s been unclear what effects these","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"forests may have on stream biodiversity. To investigate the issue, biologist Xingli Giam and colleagues studied an Indonesian oil palm plantation,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"comparing the species richness of forested streams with that of nonforested streams. Giam and colleagues found that species richness was","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"significantly higher in forested streams, a finding the researchers attribute to the role leaf litter plays in sheltering fish from predators and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"providing food resources.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["It discusses research intended to settle a debate about how agricultural yields can be increased without negative effects on water quality.","It explains the differences between stream-protection strategies used in oil palm plantations and stream-protection strategies used in other kinds of agricultural environments.","It describes findings that challenge a previously held view about how fish that inhabit streams in agricultural environments attempt to avoid predators.","It presents a study that addresses an unresolved question about the presence of forests along streams in agricultural environments."]},{"id":"ac5bf490","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Reyna Grande’s 2012 memoir The Distance Between Us. In the text, Grande reflects on a time when she and her older sister Mago were children. A Barbie is a type of doll. I begged Mago to come play with me. She wasn’t as interested in my Barbie as she had been just two months before, which made me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for. Usually, it was me doing the envying. After I pestered her relentlessly, she finally put her notebook down and came over to me. ©2012 by Reyna Grande","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Reyna Grande’s 2012 memoir The Distance Between Us. In the text, Grande reflects on a time when she and her older","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sister Mago were children. A Barbie is a type of doll.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I begged Mago to come play with me. She wasn’t as interested in my Barbie as she had been just two months before, which made","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for. Usually, it was me doing the envying. After I pestered her","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"relentlessly, she finally put her notebook down and came over to me.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©2012 by Reyna Grande","indent":4}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text?","choices":["It indicates Grande’s unhappiness over Mago’s disinterest in Grande’s doll.","It expresses Grande’s anger over Mago’s refusal to spend time with her.","It presents an example of how Mago and Grande generally played together as children.","It provides a reason for why Mago is unwilling to play with Grande."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["which made","me sad because that was the only thing Mago had envied me for."]},{"id":"af43b0bd","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Researchers have long hypothesized that woolly mammoths were hunted to extinction in North America by humans using spears with grooved tips known as Clovis points. One anthropologist set out to test this hypothesis. Using a mechanical spear-thrower, he launched spears with Clovis points into mounds of clay — substitutes for the animals large bodies. The projectiles generally penetrated only a few inches into the clay, an amount insufficient to have harmed most woolly mammoths. This led the anthropologist to conclude that hunters using spears with Clovis points likely weren’t the principal drivers of the extinction.","question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To argue for the significance of new findings amid an ongoing debate among researchers","To discuss the advantages and disadvantages of the method used in an experiment","To summarize two competing hypotheses and a major finding associated with each one","To describe an experiment whose results cast doubt on an established hypothesis"]},{"id":"47598085","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Yawn contagion occurs when one individual yawns in response to another’s yawn. Studies of this behavior in primates have focused on populations in captivity, but biologist Elisabetta Palagi and her colleagues have shown that it can occur in wild primate populations as well. In their study, which focused on a wild population of gelada monkeys (Theropithecus gelada) in Ethiopia, the researchers further reported that yawn contagion most commonly occurred in males and across different social groups instead of within a single social group.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Yawn contagion occurs when one individual yawns in response to another’s yawn. Studies of this behavior in primates have focused on","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"populations in captivity, but biologist Elisabetta Palagi and her colleagues have shown that it can occur in wild primate populations as well. In","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"their study, which focused on a wild population of gelada monkeys (Theropithecus gelada) in Ethiopia, the researchers further reported that yawn","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"contagion most commonly occurred in males and across different social groups instead of within a single social group.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It defines a phenomenon that is discussed in the text.","It introduces a problem that is examined in the text.","It makes a claim that is challenged in the text.","It presents a hypothesis that is evaluated in the text."],"underline":"Yawn contagion occurs when one individual yawns in response to anothers ’ yawn.","underline_segments":["Yawn contagion occurs when one individual yawns in response to another’s yawn."]},{"id":"ca50de52","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"“How lifelike are they?” Many computer animators prioritize this question as they strive to create ever more realistic environments and lighting. Generally, while characters in computer-animated films appear highly exaggerated, environments and lighting are carefully engineered to mimic reality. But some animators, such as Pixar’s Sanjay Patel, are focused on a different question. Rather than asking first whether the environments and lighting they’re creating are convincingly lifelike, Patel and others are asking whether these elements reflect their films’ unique stories.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"“How lifelike are they?” Many computer animators prioritize this question as they strive to create ever more realistic environments and lighting.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Generally, while characters in computer-animated films appear highly exaggerated, environments and lighting are carefully engineered to mimic","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"reality. But some animators, such as Pixar’s Sanjay Patel, are focused on a different question. Rather than asking first whether the environments","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and lighting they’re creating are convincingly lifelike, Patel and others are asking whether these elements reflect their films’ unique stories.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined question in the text as a whole?","choices":["It reflects a primary goal that many computer animators have for certain components of the animations they produce.","It represents a concern of computer animators who are more interested in creating unique backgrounds and lighting effects than realistic ones.","It conveys the uncertainty among many computer animators about how to create realistic animations using current technology.","It illustrates a reaction that audiences typically have to the appearance of characters created by computer animators."],"underline":"“How lifelike are they?”","underline_segments":["“How lifelike are they?”"]},{"id":"34d7bb25","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"According to Indian economist and sociologist Radhakamal Mukerjee (1889 – 1968), the Eurocentric concepts that informed early twentieth- century social scientific methods —for example, the idea that all social relations are reducible to struggles between individuals — had little relevance for India. Making the social sciences more responsive to Indians needs, Mukerjee argued, required constructing analytical categories informed by India’s cultural and ecological circumstances. Mukerjee thus proposed the communalist Indian village as the ideal model on which to base Indian economic and social policy.","question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["The text recounts Mukerjee’s early training in the social scientific disciplines and then lists social policies whose implementation Mukerjee oversaw.","The text mentions some of Mukerjee’s economic theories and then traces their impact on other Indian social scientists of the twentieth century.","The text presents Mukerjee’s critique of the social sciences and then provides an example of his attempts to address issues he identified in his critique.","The text explains an influential economic theory and then demonstrates how that theory was more important to Mukerjee’s work than other social scientists have acknowledged."]},{"id":"c4900368","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from the 1924 poem “Cycle” by D Arcy McNickle, who was a citizen of the Confederated Salish and Kootenai Tribes. There shall be new roads wending, A new beating of the drum — Men’s eyes shall have fresh seeing, Grey lives reprise their span — But under the new sun’s being, Completing what night began, There ll be the same backs bending, The same sad feet shall drum — When this night finds its ending And day shall have come.....","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from the 1924 poem “Cycle” by D’Arcy McNickle, who was a citizen of the Confederated Salish and Kootenai Tribes.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"There shall be new roads wending,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"A new beating of the drum—","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Men’s eyes shall have fresh seeing,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Grey lives reprise their span—","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"But under the new sun’s being,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Completing what night began,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"There’ll be the same backs bending,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The same sad feet shall drum—","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"When this night finds its ending","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"And day shall have come.....","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To consider how the repetitiveness inherent in human life can be both rewarding and challenging","To question whether activities completed at one time of day are more memorable than those completed at another time of day","To refute the idea that joy is a more commonly experienced emotion than sadness is","To demonstrate how the experiences of individuals relate to the experiences of their communities"]},{"id":"a68239ed","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Oscar Wilde’s 1897 nonfiction work De Profundis. People whose desire is solely for self-realisation never know where they are going. They can’t know. In one sense of the word it is of course necessary to know oneself: that is the first achievement of knowledge. But to recognise that the soul of a man is unknowable, is the ultimate achievement of wisdom. The final mystery is oneself. When one has weighed the sun in the balance, and measured the steps of the moon, and mapped out the seven heavens star by star, there still remains oneself. Who can calculate the orbit of his own soul?","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Oscar Wilde’s 1897 nonfiction work De Profundis.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"People whose desire is solely for self-realisation never know where they are going. They can’t know. In one sense of the word it is","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"of course necessary to know oneself: that is the first achievement of knowledge. But to recognise that the soul of a man is","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"unknowable, is the ultimate achievement of wisdom. The final mystery is oneself. When one has weighed the sun in the balance,","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"and measured the steps of the moon, and mapped out the seven heavens star by star, there still remains oneself. Who can","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"calculate the orbit of his own soul?","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined question in the text as a whole?","choices":["It reinforces the text’s skepticism about the possibility of truly achieving self-knowledge.","It speculates that some readers will share the doubts expressed in the text about the value of self-knowledge.","It cautions readers that the text’s directions for how to achieve self-knowledge are hard to follow.","It concedes that the definition of self-knowledge advanced in the text is unpopular."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["Who can","calculate the orbit of his own soul?"]},{"id":"662ebff2","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In response to concerns that some recent financial crises were exacerbated by consumers misunderstanding risks associated with credit cards, loans, and other financial products, policymakers in many countries have instituted risk-disclosure requirements on sellers of those products. Enrique Seira et al. investigated a variety of risk-disclosure messages sent to thousands of credit card customers and found that the messages had only small and short-lived effects on behavior. Seira et al. asserted that such effects may nevertheless be worth pursuing, given the negligible cost of messaging.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In response to concerns that some recent financial crises were exacerbated by consumers misunderstanding risks associated with credit cards,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"loans, and other financial products, policymakers in many countries have instituted risk-disclosure requirements on sellers of those products.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Enrique Seira et al. investigated a variety of risk-disclosure messages sent to thousands of credit card customers and found that the messages","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"had only small and short-lived effects on behavior. Seira et al. asserted that such effects may nevertheless be worth pursuing, given the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"negligible cost of messaging.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It notes a factor that led Seira et al. to not dismiss risk-disclosure messaging altogether despite their evidence of its limited utility.","It acknowledges a type of risk-disclosure messaging that Seira et al. may not have fully accounted for in their study.","It describes a consideration that explains why Seira et al. recommended risk-disclosure messaging even though its effects may be small relative to its costs.","It points out a circumstance that Seira et al. conceded may make risk-disclosure messaging more effective than their study suggests."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["given the","negligible cost of messaging."]},{"id":"7a0e31ea","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Betty Smith’s 1943 novel A Tree Grows in Brooklyn. Francie, a young girl, visits the library often. Francie thought that all the books in the world were in that library and she had a plan about reading all the books in the world. She was reading a book a day in alphabetical order and not skipping the dry ones. She remembered that the first author had been Abbott. She had been reading a book a day for a long time now and she was still in the B’s. Already she had read about bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations and Byzantine architecture. For all her enthusiasm, she had to admit that some of the B’s had been’ hard going. But Francie was a reader. ©1947 by Betty Smith","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Betty Smith’s 1943 novel A Tree Grows in Brooklyn. Francie, a young girl, visits the library often.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Francie thought that all the books in the world were in that library and she had a plan about reading all the books in the world. She","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"was reading a book a day in alphabetical order and not skipping the dry ones. She remembered that the first author had been","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Abbott. She had been reading a book a day for a long time now and she was still in the B’s. Already she had read about bees and","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"buffaloes, Bermuda vacations and Byzantine architecture. For all her enthusiasm, she had to admit that some of the B’s had been","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"hard going. But Francie was a reader.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©1947 by Betty Smith","indent":4}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To illustrate Francie’s enjoyment of an unusual topic","To explain why Francie prefers reading over other activities","To portray Francie’s determination to meet a goal","To describe a book that Francie greatly admires"]}];
